mantle rm537
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_olaf_fogstack
title the puddle post
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers warmth=warm drive=steady
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sends_little_leaf_letters_down_a_rain_runnel
likes plum_tart dice quiet_chapel warm_rain
dislikes smoke flies
fears a_note_stuck_beneath_a_grating a_quiet_visitor_left_out
hopes a_letter_boat_that_comes_back a_warm_slice_for_a_friend
topics weather +0.5 newcomer +0.4 pastimes +0.4
styles comfort=gentle gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# knows which puddles join in a downpour and likes to send a little folded leaf along each newly opened waterway.

words
oath! = Plum stones in my post | A sunk leaf on delivery
saying! = A little leaf can carry a big hello | Give the puddle a chance to answer
leafpost = my little green letter | the folded leaf
curlpoint = the curl at the stem | my curled-up prow
puddleroad = a trickle with a turn | the shining gutter road
drydock = an upside-down saucer | my waiting quay
plumcheek = a soft purple half | a shiny bit of plum
dotstone = a pebble with six spots | my pretend die
tallside = the edge without wet | a wall of dry stone
pupword = a tiny ink squiggle | a mark for hello
windhand = a push from the breeze | a little nibble of wind
quietseat = a dark wooden end | the very still seat

any
opinion dole for 3 : A wolf who's run out of bread should get some while the bread still smells good.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A wolf new to town can follow my finger to the link between puddles. It's a small thing I know that might be wanted.
opinion church for 1 : A chapel can have the kind of quiet that lets somebody finish a sad thought without having to tell it.
opinion festivals for 1 : Good to have a day for sending wishes further than the nearest puddle.
opinion times against 1 : Some days it takes an awfully long walk to find a bit of tart that we can afford.

grown

grown
line greet : My leaf has found an open reach. You're welcome beside it.
line greet.return : A sound greeting carries beyond a small stretch of water.
line again.open : Back by the little current together.
line farewell : Let the folded leaf choose its last few inches.
line farewell.return : I'll see it through the final bend.
line react.news : I'd hear the part that stayed afloat on its own.
line preclose : A little thing still needs guiding out of the weeds.

adolescent
line greet : I can see right across this channel.
line greet.return : Your voice just cleared the turning pool.
line farewell : I'll be along after the leaf makes shore.
line farewell.return : No parcel could ask a fairer wind.

young
line greet : Here comes my puddle letter. There's room to watch.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You're new. The broad puddle's only pretending to be deep.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Look how the very first light gets on my leaf.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : My little letter has a shiny evening stamp.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Let me get my lesson leaf on dry paper first.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family gets the good spot beside the bend.
line again.open : My little post keeps coming back to you.
line greet.return : I heard you over the tiny sloshing.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your hello fits on my best leaf.
line farewell : Safe home by the puddle with the shallow side.
line farewell.return : I'll say your goodbye to the letter boat.
line react.news : Which bit would fit on my folded leaf?
line react.news.new : I haven't sent that news anywhere yet.
line react.news.known : A leaf brought that bit round before.
line react.news.doubt : Was anybody standing close enough to see it splash?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can sit quietly outside the sad place a while.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd put a little purple spot on a letter for that.
line answer.how : A bit low, but there's still a leaf coming my way.
line ask.how : Has somebody done you a little kindness today?
line sympathise : I'd wait with you till the puddle stops shaking.
line reassure : My sitting stone's wide enough to share.
line decline : I promised to get this letter through the bend before taking another one.
line accept_decline : My second letter can stay behind the saucer then.
line thank : You gave my little thing a proper chance to float.
line preclose : The green point has reached the last wide puddle.
line ack : Afloat.

young

scene leaf
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold a leaf so its stalk sticks up like a letter carrier's nose.
b : What letters can it carry? | Why put the stalk up?
a : A dot means hello. Three dots mean I saved some tart if you come soon. | So a finger can tap it loose if it's stuck under the bridge of my foot.

scene flood
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two puddles that never touch can send post to each other after a shower.
b : Which puddles will join? | Do the letters come back?
a : There's a tiny groove with grit in it. When the grit begins to move, my post can get through. | Only if I carry them uphill myself. Water's got a very fixed idea about the way home.

scene lessons
when topic=work self.job=child self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make all the letters of a short word fit on a big leaf now.
b : Which word? | Does the ink run?
a : Home. A letter with that address has a very good reason to keep going. | I use a bit of pale chalk. It only needs to last to the next crossing.

scene tart
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plum tart has two little pockets if you divide it right where the fruit goes round.
b : Do you get first pick? | Would you send a piece with the post?
a : I'll wait for the other wolf to choose. The tart tastes better when somebody's there. | No, the leaf might sink and I don't think a puddle has properly earned plum tart.

scene dice
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put spots on a pebble so I could play a game without owning another die.
b : Can you roll a round pebble? | How can it show a six?
a : Very well indeed. Stopping in a particular place is the part it hasn't learned. | I made one flat side and put all six spots there. It's a lucky pebble for a beginner.

scene chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a quiet chapel I can hear the rolled edge of my sleeve brushing the seat.
b : Does that sound big? | Do you sit there alone?
a : Much bigger than outside. I smooth the edge when my own thoughts want listening to. | Sometimes. Quiet works with company too if both wolves are content to listen.

scene warmrain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm shower can make a whole street ready for my leaf post before my coat's cold.
b : Do you hurry out? | Is the leaf warm too?
a : I watch which water has grit moving in it first. It's no good hurrying a letter onto dry stone. | My fingers think so. It doesn't curl itself against my wrist like a cold leaf.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoke in my eyes makes it appear I've gone all sorry about an ordinary little leaf.
b : Are you really crying? | What helps?
a : Sometimes water comes out without asking my feelings. I can tell which sort of tears they are. | Moving into clear air and waiting without rubbing. There's a dry sleeve if I need one.

scene fly
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly on my letter's getting a free ride and hasn't even opened the post.
b : Will the letter sink? | Could you charge the fly?
a : Only if it brings all its relations. A good leaf will float a little speck. | I'd charge one promise to stay clear of my plum when we get there.

scene mum
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think #self.mother# would have a fine leaf with a clear road to take it home.
b : What would you write? | Can you send it that far?
a : A little round mark that means I'm thinking about home. I've got other marks for wanting supper. | The water takes it partway. The rest of the delivery belongs to me.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hope #self.friend# might pick my first stamp for my post.
b : Which stamp would you pick? | Must every stamp be round?
a : A twig drawn like a little fork. It means there's a choice of ways ahead. | Any shape you can make on a leaf while it's still holding steady.

scene sump
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Sump some of the smallest gutters know all the big streets by name.
b : Can they talk? | How do you know?
a : They tell my leaf which way to go. A quick leaf can get quite a lot said without a mouth. | I watch where the water comes out. A puddle that starts there can run right under two other streets.

scene secret
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know that a grown wolf can need a quiet corner just as much as a pup.
b : Would you tell who? | Could you help?
a : I'd keep that particular letter shut. Another wolf ought to choose when a private face gets seen. | I'd give the corner a bit of space and make sure no one stepped straight into it.

scene cheap
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fallen leaf is a whole fresh sheet nobody asks a copper for.
b : Can you use a torn one? | What about the stem?
a : Two little notes instead of one big one. I can find something to say to either half. | That's the clever bit that keeps a parcel from rolling after it's landed on the saucer.

scene shadow
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My leaf gets to a lamp circle and seems to turn silver a moment.
b : Can you still read the mark? | What happens outside the light?
a : The dark little dot shows even better than before for that one shining bit. | I can hear the tail of the leaf brush the side. Then I'd like a friend with sharp eyes.

scene lost
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A visitor can ask me which puddle will top an ordinary pair of shoes.
b : Will you show the dry way? | Is it a very big puddle?
a : Yes, with a finger pointing. I learned on my own socks and you don't need to. | Big enough to surprise a wolf who only looked at the shallow side.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm hoping for a letter from a puddle higher up than mine.
b : Who would write it? | What would you send back?
a : Some other wolf who likes fitting a message on a leaf. We could get quite friendly that way. | A leaf carried up in my pocket, with a mark saying the next shower can bring another.

adolescent

scene fountain
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can guide a folded leaf round an entire little basin before the stem gets soft.
b : How do you turn it? | Could a heavier parcel go?
a : A breath just beyond the leaf is usually enough. Blowing down on it sinks the message. | A thread perhaps. Water has a rather strict allowance for a private post.

scene longname
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I write shorter addresses now instead of trying to squeeze every letter into a small space.
b : Which words do you leave? | Is it easier?
a : I keep the ones the carrier needs to find a particular door. Most of my explaining can go inside. | Easier on the reader, which is an excellent return for a bit of thought.

scene quietage
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's still a point in a quiet visit when I'd prefer company kept its questions for later.
b : How would somebody tell? | Would you stay long?
a : I should say so kindly. There's no great shame in asking for a little room to finish a thought. | Until I could take a cheerful interest in the walk home.

grown

scene oldpost
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A leaf afloat on a stone channel can recall a whole private postal service to me.
b : What did it deliver? | Who received the messages?
a : Small marks of considerable importance to a pup with two wet socks. | Whoever happened to be watching when the leaf arrived. No signature required for receipt.

scene font
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still find a pocket of quiet between the sounds coming in from a busy street.
b : Where would you find one? | Could I sit with you?
a : Almost any chapel seat when the door's done swinging and my own ears have settled. | Please. A companion who sits easily can enlarge a quiet place.

scene bridge
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a flooded crossing by the speed of a light thing along its edge.
b : Why the edge? | Would you step in to test it?
a : That's the part visible from safe stone. I'm not putting either foot in to satisfy an idle question. | I'd choose a higher crossing if the answer was doubtful.

scene plumready
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The neatest way to share a plum tart is to let the second portion choose itself.
b : How can a portion choose? | What if your cut was uneven?
a : I cut, the guest chooses, and the half that's left becomes mine. | I've given myself an excellent reason to pay attention when dividing the next tart.

scene help
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Showing a stranger dry footing is a gift which costs precisely a moment of looking.
b : Even if either wolf's hurrying? | Which details would you show?
a : A moment is often less than the time two wet boots would take to dry. | The shallow lip, the high step and the place where one's view of the channel is deceiving.

scene flies
when topic=food self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've learned to cover sweet things with a cloth before letting the weather claim my attention.
b : Does it keep every fly away? | Would a lid serve?
a : Enough to let a guest choose a slice in peace. I ask a modest return on the effort. | Yes, if it clears the fruit without touching. My idea is protection, not a second crust.

scene tone
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A report can be passed along with its dry meaning quite washed away.
b : How can that happen? | Can it be recovered?
a : Each teller adds a little flourish till the original mark gets hard to recognise. | Ask somebody who saw the original thing. Otherwise keep the guess at its actual size.

scene springwet
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spring shower still has the power to call me away from a very sensible indoor occupation.
b : What would you watch? | Does the occupation wait?
a : The first water making its own way between two separate hollows. I've always liked the instant they join. | If I've finished my share. Growing up taught me something about the price of wet sleeves.

scene motherthought
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sometimes think of the little marks I meant for #self.mother# when I address a proper sheet of paper.
b : Do those marks still have a use? | What does a mark say?
a : In a private margin on a suitable occasion. A serious paper is welcome to keep its proper form. | I remembered the way home, even on the days when each turning was an adventure.

scene kindness
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer to give a distressed wolf a useful small courtesy before asking about all the circumstances.
b : What courtesy? | What if no account follows?
a : A seat clear of passersby, or a little water within reach. That leaves both of us a choice. | The courtesy will still have reached the right address.

scene tired
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good long look at running water sometimes rests my eyes better than shutting them.
b : Why would that be? | Would a trickle do?
a : It asks my sight to follow one simple thing while everything else on today's list slips gently away. | A trickle's excellent. Its small scale was part of the original attraction.

scene dicegrown
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy dice when every face can show in the same clear patch of light.
b : Do you insist on a flat board? | What do you wager?
a : Certainly. A sloping table can win without ever having taken a turn of its own. | A small courtesy, perhaps the choice of a filling for tomorrow's tart.

young

story leaflost [topic=weather]
  : I put my best leaf in a puddle and looked up to see who'd be round the corner to receive it.
  : When I looked down the leaf was gone and a little wet line went straight into the dry grass.
  b : Did it sink there?
  : It had rolled up on the grass and opened itself. That's a very quick way of delivering a letter.

story pips [topic=pastimes]
  : I tried to give my pebble die another spot with purple juice from my tart.
  : It made one purple spot and then another on my finger and one on my nearest whisker.
  b : Did you count them all?
  : I counted only the pebble. My nose hasn't got a flat side to play with.

story chapelquiet [topic=faith]
  : I sat so still on a chapel seat I could hear something ticking under my cuff.
  : A tiny grain of grit was rubbing against a wooden button every time I took a breath.
  b : Did you shake it away?
  : I took it outside in my sleeve. It was making the only noise and I didn't want to frighten it.

young

rule @post
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leaf post through the little channel. | First puddle's joined the second now.

rule @lesson
when concept=bark self.job=child self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Just room for the last letter. | Fresh side up for the next small word.

rule @fruit
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One purple half for the guest. | No fly gets my good plum.

rule @light
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Silver stamp in the lamplight. | That's the post's last little turning.

young
dlg resident.hub : I've a leaf letter waiting for its first good puddle. You can see the mark.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The little post knows this stop, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'd keep my leaf by the stem while we speak.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : There's just a silver edge where the water moves. We can watch it from this step.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like learning words small enough for a leaf.
dlg resident.job : I send tiny notes and look after the shallow crossing.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : There's something to put on a new leaf. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Use our dry route for the sake of your socks.

young

graft @leafstreet resident.hub
choice Who delivers your letters? -> leafstreet
node leafstreet
say The leaf does most of it and the water takes the turns. I stand by the very wet bit in case a good message gets stuck on a root.
choice How can you tell that the message arrived? -> leafstreet_more
choice Watch the leaf again. -> hub
node leafstreet_more
say When the leaf turns in the last little pool I pick it up and deliver it overland from there. My feet finish the dry journey.
choice Watch the leaf again. -> hub
choice Take the high crossing. -> bye
